7.6.m:
being comforted and consoled, he did not perform the water rite; / and he of great austerity made this vow in the midst of the seers, / difficult to perform for all living beings, having sipped water with joined palms: / "From this day forward, I shall not draw breath in any way;
the vital airs abiding in my body shall never move. / Deprived of blinking and opening my eyes, standing on one foot with raised arms, / having become like wood, a clod of earth, or stone, I shall remain, without doubt, / as long as I do not see Rudra and likewise as long as I do not see my father.
Until I behold him together with his wife, this is my vow."

